{
  "id": "selkov-basic-glycolysis-biology",
  "name": "Basic Selkov glycolysis near a stable positive state",
  "description": "Normalized basic Selkov system, distinct from the saturated five-species derivation. Here alpha0.8<1/(gamma-1) and the local positive equilibrium is stable. The source proves unbounded behavior for other regimes; no universal boundedness claim. Illustrative gamma2,alpha0.8 and initial(1.2,0.8) chosen near stable(1,1); normalized coefficients1. Horizon50 and RK4dt0.025 are verification choices. Mathematical source article CC BY4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Signed net-rate flows encode equations, not material transfer claims. No clamps or hidden state resets.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00285-021-01560-y",
  "reference": "Brechmann and Rendall (2021), Unbounded solutions of models for glycolysis, Eqs9-10; original Selkov (1968), doi:10.1111/j.1432-1033.1968.tb00175.x.",
